PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L05U4.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":5,"cefr":"B1a","unit":4,"theme":"Our Planet","essential_question":"What will happen to our planet if we don't change our habits?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1","title":"If We Act Now, We Will Save Our Planet: The First Conditional and unless","objectives":["Students will be able to use the first conditional to talk about real possibilities in the future and their results.","Students will be able to use unless to mean \"if… not\".","I can say \"If we recycle, we will reduce waste.\"","I can say \"Unless we act now, the leopard will disappear.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الجملة الشرطية الأولى للتحدث عن احتمالات حقيقية في المستقبل ونتائجها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام unless بمعنى «إذا لم».","أستطيع أن أقول If we recycle, we will reduce waste.","أستطيع أن أقول Unless we act now, the leopard will disappear."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"environment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","definition":"the air, water and land around us where people, animals and plants live","arabic":"البيئة","example":"We must keep our environment clean.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W01"},{"word":"pollution","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈluʃən/","definition":"dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land","arabic":"التلوّث","example":"Car fumes cause air pollution in big cities.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W02"},{"word":"recycle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"to treat used things so they can be used again","arabic":"يعيد التدوير","example":"We recycle paper and cans at school.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W03"},{"word":"waste","pos":"noun","ipa":"/weɪst/","definition":"things we throw away because we don't need them","arabic":"النفايات / الهدر","example":"Restaurants produce a lot of food waste.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"The first conditional talks about a real possibility in the future and its result: If we plant more trees, the air will be cleaner.\nForm: If + present simple, will / won't + base verb. We do NOT use will in the if-clause: (not: If it will rain…) → If it rains… The two clauses can change places: The air will be cleaner if we plant more trees.\nunless = if… not. Unless we recycle, the waste will grow. = If we don't recycle, the waste will grow. After unless, use a positive verb: (not: Unless we don't recycle).\nIf + present simple, will/won't + base verb\nresult clause first: will + base verb + if + present simple\nno will in the if-clause\nunless = if not (positive verb after unless)","examples":["If we recycle paper, we'll save trees.","The fish will die if the water gets too dirty.","If you leave the lights on, you'll waste electricity.","Unless we act now, the Arabian leopard will disappear.","If it doesn't rain this winter, there'll be a drought.","We won't have clean beaches if people drop litter.","What will you do if you see someone throwing plastic in the sea?","If the school buys solar panels, it will reduce its electricity bill."],"common_errors":["✗ If it will rain, we will stay home. → ✓ If it rains, we will stay home. (No will in the if-clause.)","✗ If we recycle, we save the planet tomorrow. → ✓ If we recycle, we will save the planet. (Future result → will.)","✗ Unless we don't conserve water, we will have problems. → ✓ Unless we conserve water, we will have problems. (unless = if not → positive verb.)","✗ If you will drop litter, the beach will be dirty. → ✓ If you drop litter, the beach will be dirty. (If + present simple.)"],"arabic":"الجملة الشرطية الأولى لاحتمال حقيقي في المستقبل ونتيجته: If we plant more trees, the air will be cleaner.\nالصيغة: If + المضارع البسيط، will + المصدر. لا نستخدم will بعد if.\nunless تعني «إذا لم»، ويأتي بعدها فعل مثبت: Unless we recycle = If we don't recycle.\nيمكن تقديم جملة النتيجة: The air will be cleaner if we plant more trees."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If We Act Now, We Will Save Our Planet: The First Conditional and unless”. Let’s learn first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U4-LS1 | If We Act Now, We Will Save Our Planet: The First Conditional and unless","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “The Eco Club Speech”: Good morning, everyone! I'm Adam, the president of our school Eco Club, and today I want to talk about our planet. If we don't change our habits, our environment will suffer. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Good morning, everyone! I'm Adam, the president of our school Eco Club, and today I want to talk about our planet. If we don't change our habits, our environment will suffer.","visual":"Image GV-L05-U4-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"The first conditional talks about a real possibility in the future and its result: If we plant more trees, the air will be cleaner. Form: If + present simple, will / won't + base verb. We do NOT use will in the if-clause: (not: If it will rain…) → If it rains… The two clauses can change places: The air will be cleaner if we plant more trees.","on_screen":"If + present simple, will/won't + base verb • result clause first: will + base verb + if + present simple • no will in the if-clause","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. If we recycle paper, we'll save trees. The fish will die if the water gets too dirty. If you leave the lights on, you'll waste electricity.","on_screen":"If we recycle paper, we'll save trees. / The fish will die if the water gets too dirty. / If you leave the lights on, you'll waste electricity.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If it will rain, we will stay home.” That’s not right. We say: “If it rains, we will stay home.” No will in the if-clause.","on_screen":"✗ If it will rain, we will stay home.   ✓ If it rains, we will stay home.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner.\" Is this possible? … Think! … Yes – it's a real possibility. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"If we recycle, we will reduce waste.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"If we recycle, we will reduce waste.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة الشرطية الأولى لاحتمال حقيقي في المستقبل ونتيجته: If we plant more trees, the air will be cleaner.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If it will rain, we will stay home. — الصحيح: If it rains, we will stay home.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول If we recycle, we will reduce waste."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Eco Club Speech","body":"Good morning, everyone! I'm Adam, the president of our school Eco Club, and today I want to talk about our planet.\nIf we don't change our habits, our environment will suffer.\nSaudi Arabia has a dry climate with very little rain. If we waste water, we will face serious problems in the future.\nSo please turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. If everyone does this, we'll save thousands of liters every year.\nPlastic is another problem. If you bring a reusable bottle to school, you won't need plastic ones.\nOur club has a plan: we'll put recycling bins in every classroom. Unless we recycle, our school will produce tons of waste.\nAlso, if we plant more trees, they'll give us shade and cleaner air.\nRemember: if each of us makes one small change, we will make a big difference. Thank you!","word_count":144,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"If we ___ paper, we'll save trees.","options":["recycle","will recycle","recycling","recycled"],"answer":"recycle","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"If you leave the tap on, you ___ a lot of water.","options":["wasted","waste","will waste","wasting"],"answer":"will waste","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."},{"q":"___ we protect its habitat, the Arabian leopard will disappear.","options":["Unless","If","So","When"],"answer":"Unless","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"The beach ___ clean if people drop litter.","options":["doesn't stay","won't stays","not stay","won't stay"],"answer":"won't stay","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."},{"q":"What will happen if the oceans ___ warmer?","options":["got","get","will get","getting"],"answer":"get","explanation":"Questions: What will happen if…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"Unless we ___ water, we'll have a serious shortage.","options":["don't conserve","will conserve","conserve","conserving"],"answer":"conserve","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: stop, will be, doesn't rain","items":[{"q":"If it ______ (not / rain) this year, the farmers will lose their crops.","options":[],"answer":"doesn't rain","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"The air ______ (be) cleaner if we use more electric buses.","options":[],"answer":"will be","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."},{"q":"Unless people ______ (stop) hunting them, these birds will become extinct.","options":[],"answer":"stop","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite with unless.","items":[{"q":"If we don't reduce plastic, the sea will be full of it.  (unless)","options":[],"answer":"Unless we reduce plastic, the sea will be full of it.","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"If you don't turn off the lights, you'll waste energy.  (unless)","options":[],"answer":"Unless you turn off the lights, you'll waste energy.","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"If the town doesn't plant trees, it will be very hot.  (unless)","options":[],"answer":"Unless the town plants trees, it will be very hot.","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the sentences about the environment.","items":[{"q":"If we plant more trees, ___.","options":[],"answer":"If we plant more trees, the air will be cleaner.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"If people drop litter in the desert, ___.","options":[],"answer":"If people drop litter in the desert, animals will eat it and get sick.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Unless we save water, ___.","options":[],"answer":"Unless we save water, there won't be enough for everyone.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The planet will be healthier if ___.","options":[],"answer":"The planet will be healthier if we use renewable energy.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What will you do if you see a dirty beach?","options":[],"answer":"If I see a dirty beach, I'll collect the litter.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Eco promises.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 first-conditional promises for your home.","options":[],"answer":"If I turn off the lights, we'll save electricity. If I take shorter showers, I'll conserve water. If we sort our rubbish, we'll recycle more.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 warnings with unless.","options":[],"answer":"Unless we protect the oryx, it will disappear again. Unless people stop wasting food, landfills will grow.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a chain story: each result becomes the next condition (3 sentences).","options":[],"answer":"If we use less plastic, there will be less waste. If there is less waste, the sea will be cleaner. If the sea is cleaner, the turtles will be safe.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"If we recycle…"},{"label":"If you waste water…"},{"label":"Unless we act…"},{"label":"When I grow up…"},{"label":"As soon as I get home…"},{"label":"If it doesn't rain…"},{"label":"We won't… unless…"},{"label":"Before you leave…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"If the factory ___ smoke, the air will be dirty.","options":["produced","will produce","producing","produces"],"answer":"produces","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"We ___ the oryx unless we protect its habitat.","options":["don't save","not save","won't save","won't saving"],"answer":"won't save","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."},{"q":"","options":["If it rains tomorrow, we'll plant the trees on Sunday.","If it rained tomorrow, we'll plant the trees on Sunday.","If it will rain tomorrow, we'll plant the trees on Sunday.","If it rains tomorrow, we plant the trees on Sunday yesterday."],"answer":"If it rains tomorrow, we'll plant the trees on Sunday.","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["Unless you watered the plants, they'll die.","Unless you will water the plants, they'll die.","Unless you water the plants, they'll die.","Unless you don't water the plants, they'll die."],"answer":"Unless you water the plants, they'll die.","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"What ___ you do if you find an injured bird?","options":["are","do","did","will"],"answer":"will","explanation":"Questions: What will happen if…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"\"Unless we act now\" means ___.","options":["If we don't act now","If we act now","Because we act now","When we act now"],"answer":"If we don't act now","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"","options":["The turtles will be safe if we keep the beaches clean.","The turtles will be safe if we kept the beaches clean.","The turtles will be safe if we will keep the beaches clean.","The turtles are safe tomorrow if we keep the beaches clean."],"answer":"The turtles will be safe if we keep the beaches clean.","explanation":"The clauses can change order.","explanation_ar":"يمكن تبديل ترتيب الجملتين."},{"q":"If you ___ a reusable bag, you won't need plastic ones.","options":["will bring","brought","bringing","bring"],"answer":"bring","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"If we don't conserve energy, our bills ___ higher.","options":["getting","will get","got","get"],"answer":"will get","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."},{"q":"Which sentence is a first conditional?","options":["We are recycling cans now.","If we recycle cans, we'll reduce waste.","We recycled cans last week.","We have recycled many cans."],"answer":"If we recycle cans, we'll reduce waste.","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Adam giving a speech on the school stage in front of a large Earth poster, with recycling bins, a dripping tap and a young tree in a pot beside him; Zaki the Falcon holding a sign \"Our Planet, Our Future\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam giving a speech on the school stage in front of a large Earth poster, with recycling bins, a dripping tap and a young tree in a pot beside him; Zaki the Falcon holding a sign \"Our Planet, Our Future\""},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows environment (the air, water and land around us where people, animals and plants live); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing environment: the air, water and land around us where people, animals and plants live"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows pollution (dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing pollution: dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows recycle (to treat used things so they can be used again); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing recycle: to treat used things so they can be used again"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows waste (things we throw away because we don't need them); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing waste: things we throw away because we don't need them"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W01","script":"environment. environment. We must keep our environment clean.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W02","script":"pollution. pollution. Car fumes cause air pollution in big cities.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W03","script":"recycle. recycle. We recycle paper and cans at school.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-W04","script":"waste. waste. Restaurants produce a lot of food waste.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-T1","script":"Good morning, everyone! I'm Adam, the president of our school Eco Club, and today I want to talk about our planet. If we don't change our habits, our environment will suffer. Saudi Arabia has a dry climate with very little rain. If we waste water, we will face serious problems in the future. So please turn off the tap while you brush your teeth. If everyone does this, we'll save thousands of liters every year. Plastic is another problem. If you bring a reusable bottle to school, you won't need plastic ones. Our club has a plan: we'll put recycling bins in every classroom. Unless we recycle, our school will produce tons of waste. Also, if we plant more trees, they'll give us shade and cleaner air. Remember: if each of us makes one small change, we will make a big difference. Thank you!","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If We Act Now, We Will Save Our Planet: The First Conditional and unless”. Let’s learn first conditional (If + present simple, will + base verb) for real future possibilities; unless = if not together. Listen to the start of “The Eco Club Speech”: Good morning, everyone! I'm Adam, the president of our school Eco Club, and today I want to talk about our planet. If we don't change our habits, our environment will suffer. Look at the green words. The first conditional talks about a real possibility in the future and its result: If we plant more trees, the air will be cleaner. Form: If + present simple, will / won't + base verb. We do NOT use will in the if-clause: (not: If it will rain…) → If it rains… The two clauses can change places: The air will be cleaner if we plant more trees. Here are some examples. If we recycle paper, we'll save trees. The fish will die if the water gets too dirty. If you leave the lights on, you'll waste electricity. Be careful! Some learners say: “If it will rain, we will stay home.” That’s not right. We say: “If it rains, we will stay home.” No will in the if-clause. Quick check: \"If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner.\" Is this possible? … Think! … Yes – it's a real possibility. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"If we recycle, we will reduce waste.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2","title":"When the Rain Comes… When vs if and Future Time Clauses","objectives":["Students will be able to choose when for things that are sure to happen and if for things that might happen.","Students will be able to use the present simple (not will) after when, as soon as, before, after and until with a future meaning.","I can say \"When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish.\"","I can say \"We'll wait until the rain stops.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار when لما هو مؤكد الحدوث وif لما قد يحدث.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المضارع البسيط (وليس will) بعد when وas soon as وbefore وafter وuntil بمعنى المستقبل.","أستطيع أن أقول When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish.","أستطيع أن أقول We'll wait until the rain stops."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"protect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prəˈtɛkt/","definition":"to keep something safe from harm","arabic":"يحمي","example":"Rangers protect the animals in the reserve.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W01"},{"word":"endangered","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɛnˈdeɪndʒɚd/","definition":"at risk of disappearing forever","arabic":"مهدَّد بالانقراض","example":"The Arabian leopard is an endangered animal.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W02"},{"word":"species","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈspiʃiz/","definition":"a group of animals or plants of the same kind","arabic":"نوع / فصيلة","example":"Scientists found a new species of lizard.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W03"},{"word":"habitat","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbəˌtæt/","definition":"the natural home of an animal or plant","arabic":"موطن طبيعي","example":"The desert is the habitat of the Arabian oryx.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use when for something you are sure will happen: When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish. (I will get home.) Use if for something that might happen: If it rains, we'll plant the trees. (Maybe it will rain.)\nAfter the time words when, as soon as, before, after, until, use the present simple for the future – NOT will: We'll clean the yard as soon as the bell rings. (NOT (not: as soon as the bell will ring))\nas soon as = immediately when. until = up to the time when: We'll wait until the rain stops. Use a comma when the time clause comes first: Before you leave, turn off the lights.\nwhen = sure • if = possible\nwhen / as soon as / before / after / until + present simple (future meaning)\nmain clause: will / won't / imperative\nNot: When I will finish… → When I finish…","examples":["When I grow up, I'll become an environmental scientist.","If I see litter, I'll pick it up.","As soon as the bell rings, we'll clean the yard.","Before you leave the room, turn off the air conditioner.","We'll plant the seeds after the rain stops.","Don't throw the bottle away until you find a recycling bin.","When the sun comes up, the solar panels will start working.","If the project succeeds, other schools will copy it."],"common_errors":["✗ When I will get home, I will recycle the cans. → ✓ When I get home, I will recycle the cans. (After when → present simple.)","✗ We'll wait until the rain will stop. → ✓ We'll wait until the rain stops. (After until → present simple.)","✗ If the sun rises tomorrow, we'll start the trip. → ✓ When the sun rises tomorrow, we'll start the trip. (Sure to happen → when.)","✗ As soon as she arrives she will call you. → ✓ As soon as she arrives, she will call you. (Time clause first → comma.)"],"arabic":"when لما هو مؤكد الحدوث: When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish. وif لما قد يحدث: If it rains, we'll stay inside.\nبعد when وas soon as وbefore وafter وuntil نستخدم المضارع البسيط بمعنى المستقبل، وليس will.\nas soon as = بمجرد أن، وuntil = حتى.\nإذا بدأت الجملة بجملة الزمن نضع فاصلة بعدها."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “When the Rain Comes… When vs if and Future Time Clauses”. Let’s learn when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U4-LS2 | When the Rain Comes… When vs if and Future Time Clauses","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: As soon as I finish my homework, I'll help you. We won't leave until the teacher arrives. What will you do when you grow up?","on_screen":"As soon as I finish my homework, I'll help you. | We won't leave until the teacher arrives. | What will you do when you grow up?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use when for something you are sure will happen: When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish. (I will get home.) Use if for something that might happen: If it rains, we'll plant the trees. (Maybe it will rain.) After the time words when, as soon as, before, after, until, use the present simple for the future – NOT will: We'll clean the yard as soon as the bell rings. (NOT (not: as soon as the bell will ring))","on_screen":"when = sure • if = possible • when / as soon as / before / after / until + present simple (future meaning) • main clause: will / won't / imperative","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. When I grow up, I'll become an environmental scientist. If I see litter, I'll pick it up. As soon as the bell rings, we'll clean the yard.","on_screen":"When I grow up, I'll become an environmental scientist. / If I see litter, I'll pick it up. / As soon as the bell rings, we'll clean the yard.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “When I will get home, I will recycle the cans.” That’s not right. We say: “When I get home, I will recycle the cans.” After when → present simple.","on_screen":"✗ When I will get home, I will recycle the cans.   ✓ When I get home, I will recycle the cans.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"When I grow up…\" – will I grow up? … Think! … Yes – it's certain. Use *when*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","when لما هو مؤكد الحدوث: When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish. وif لما قد يحدث: If it rains, we'll stay inside.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: When I will get home, I will recycle the cans. — الصحيح: When I get home, I will recycle the cans.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"___ I grow up, I'll work for an environmental group.","options":["When","Unless","If","Until"],"answer":"When","explanation":"Sure to happen → when.","explanation_ar":"المؤكد ← when."},{"q":"___ it's sunny tomorrow, we'll clean the beach.","options":["When","Until","Before","If"],"answer":"If","explanation":"Might happen → if.","explanation_ar":"المحتمل ← if."},{"q":"As soon as the guests ___, we'll start the recycling fair.","options":["arrived","arrive","arriving","will arrive"],"answer":"arrive","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Don't leave ___ you've switched off the computer.","options":["if","until","as soon as","when"],"answer":"until","explanation":"until = up to the time when.","explanation_ar":"until حتى."},{"q":"Before you ___ the classroom, close the windows.","options":["leaving","left","leave","will leave"],"answer":"leave","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"When the summer holiday starts, my family ___ to Abha.","options":["will travel","travel","traveled","travels next week"],"answer":"will travel","explanation":"Main clause → will / won't / imperative.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة ← will."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Complete with the correct form. Word bank: stops, get, will present","items":[{"q":"We'll plant the trees after the rain ______ (stop).","options":[],"answer":"stops","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"As soon as I ______ (get) my allowance, I'll buy a reusable bottle.","options":[],"answer":"get","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"When we finish the project, we ______ (present) it to the principal.","options":[],"answer":"will present","explanation":"Main clause → will / won't / imperative.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة ← will."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"When I will finish school, I'll study biology.","options":[],"answer":"When I finish school, I'll study biology.","explanation":"will finish → finish. After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will finish → finish. بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"We'll stay inside until the dust storm will end.","options":[],"answer":"We'll stay inside until the dust storm ends.","explanation":"will end → ends. until = up to the time when.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: will end → ends. until حتى."},{"q":"If the sun sets tonight, the street lights will turn on.","options":[],"answer":"When the sun sets tonight, the street lights will turn on.","explanation":"If → When. Sure to happen → when.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: If → When. المؤكد ← when."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete about your future.","items":[{"q":"When I grow up, ___.","options":[],"answer":"When I grow up, I'll be a marine biologist.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"As soon as I get home today, ___.","options":[],"answer":"As soon as I get home today, I'll sort the plastic bottles.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"If I have free time this weekend, ___.","options":[],"answer":"If I have free time this weekend, I'll go hiking with my father.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Before I go to bed tonight, ___.","options":[],"answer":"Before I go to bed tonight, I'll turn off all the lights.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I won't stop trying until ___.","options":[],"answer":"I won't stop trying until I win the science competition.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Green Week plan.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your class's Green Week plan with as soon as, before and after.","options":[],"answer":"As soon as the week starts, we'll put bins in the corridors. Before we go home, we'll check the taps. After we collect the bottles, we'll take them to the recycling center.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences: one with when (sure) and one with if (possible).","options":[],"answer":"When the week ends, we'll count the bottles. If we collect 1,000 bottles, we'll win a prize.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one instruction with until.","options":[],"answer":"Don't throw away the cans until you rinse them.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"if / we / plant trees / the air / be cleaner"},{"cue":"if / you / leave the tap on / you / waste water"},{"cue":"unless / we / recycle / the landfill / grow"},{"cue":"when / I / get home / I / sort the rubbish"},{"cue":"as soon as / the bell / ring / we / clean the yard"},{"cue":"if / it / not / rain / the farmers / have problems"},{"cue":"we / not / save the leopard / unless / we / protect its habitat"},{"cue":"before / you / leave / turn off the lights"},{"cue":"if / everyone / help / we / make a difference"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"___ the bell rings, we'll go out to plant the trees.","options":["As soon as","Unless","Until","If not"],"answer":"As soon as","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["When I finish the report, I send it to you yesterday.","When I finished the report, I'll send it to you.","When I finish the report, I'll send it to you.","When I will finish the report, I'll send it to you."],"answer":"When I finish the report, I'll send it to you.","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"I'll wait here ___ the bus comes.","options":["as soon","until","unless","if not"],"answer":"until","explanation":"until = up to the time when.","explanation_ar":"until حتى."},{"q":"___ I see a falcon in the wild, I'll take a photo. (Maybe I will.)","options":["When","Before","Until","If"],"answer":"If","explanation":"Might happen → if.","explanation_ar":"المحتمل ← if."},{"q":"___ Ramadan comes, we'll donate food to families in need.","options":["Until","Unless","When","If"],"answer":"When","explanation":"Sure to happen → when.","explanation_ar":"المؤكد ← when."},{"q":"After we ___ the park, we'll have lunch.","options":["cleaning","will clean","cleaned","clean"],"answer":"clean","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["Before throw you it away, check if it's recyclable.","Before you throw it away, check if it's recyclable.","Before you will throw it away, check if it's recyclable.","Before you threw it away, check if it's recyclable."],"answer":"Before you throw it away, check if it's recyclable.","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"As soon as the solar panels arrive, the workers ___ them on the roof.","options":["puts","will put","putting","put yesterday"],"answer":"will put","explanation":"Main clause → will / won't / imperative.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة ← will."},{"q":"Which word means \"immediately when\"?","options":["until","before","as soon as","unless"],"answer":"as soon as","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["We won't go home until we finish the cleanup.","We don't go home until we finished the cleanup.","We won't go home until we will finish the cleanup.","We won't go home until finish we the cleanup."],"answer":"We won't go home until we finish the cleanup.","explanation":"until = up to the time when.","explanation_ar":"until حتى."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A school calendar for the Green Week: Monday \"Clean the yard as soon as the bell rings\", Wednesday \"Plant trees after the rain\", Thursday \"Recycling fair – when the visitors arrive\"; Omar and Yusuf carrying a young tree. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school calendar for the Green Week: Monday \"Clean the yard as soon as the bell rings\", Wednesday \"Plant trees after the rain\", Thursday \"Recycling fair – when the visitors arrive\"; Omar and Yusuf carrying a young tree"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Our Planet”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of when (certain) vs if (possible)"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows protect (to keep something safe from harm); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing protect: to keep something safe from harm"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows endangered (at risk of disappearing forever); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing endangered: at risk of disappearing forever"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows species (a group of animals or plants of the same kind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing species: a group of animals or plants of the same kind"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows habitat (the natural home of an animal or plant); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing habitat: the natural home of an animal or plant"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W01","script":"protect. protect. Rangers protect the animals in the reserve.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W02","script":"endangered. endangered. The Arabian leopard is an endangered animal.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W03","script":"species. species. Scientists found a new species of lizard.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-W04","script":"habitat. habitat. The desert is the habitat of the Arabian oryx.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “When the Rain Comes… When vs if and Future Time Clauses”. Let’s learn when (certain) vs if (possible); future time clauses with when, as soon as, before, after, until + present simple together. Remember these patterns: As soon as I finish my homework, I'll help you. We won't leave until the teacher arrives. What will you do when you grow up? Use when for something you are sure will happen: When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish. (I will get home.) Use if for something that might happen: If it rains, we'll plant the trees. (Maybe it will rain.) After the time words when, as soon as, before, after, until, use the present simple for the future – NOT will: We'll clean the yard as soon as the bell rings. (NOT (not: as soon as the bell will ring)) Here are some examples. When I grow up, I'll become an environmental scientist. If I see litter, I'll pick it up. As soon as the bell rings, we'll clean the yard. Be careful! Some learners say: “When I will get home, I will recycle the cans.” That’s not right. We say: “When I get home, I will recycle the cans.” After when → present simple. Quick check: \"When I grow up…\" – will I grow up? … Think! … Yes – it's certain. Use *when*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"When I get home, I'll sort the rubbish.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3","title":"Pollute, Pollution, Polluted: Environment Word Families","objectives":["Students will be able to use environment vocabulary to describe problems and solutions.","Students will be able to choose the correct word-family form (noun, verb, adjective, adverb) in context.","I can talk about environmental problems and solutions.","I can change \"protect\" into \"protection\" and \"recycle\" into \"recyclable\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام مفردات البيئة لوصف المشكلات والحلول.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار الصيغة الصحيحة من عائلة الكلمة (اسم، فعل، صفة، ظرف) في السياق.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن مشكلات البيئة وحلولها.","أستطيع أن أحوّل protect إلى protection وrecycle إلى recyclable."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"climate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈklaɪmət/","definition":"the usual weather in a place over a long time","arabic":"المناخ","example":"Saudi Arabia has a hot, dry climate.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W01"},{"word":"renewable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/riˈnuəbəl/","definition":"coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind","arabic":"متجدّد","example":"Solar power is a renewable form of energy.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W02"},{"word":"reduce","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rəˈdus/","definition":"to make something smaller or less","arabic":"يقلّل","example":"Please reduce the amount of plastic you use.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W03"},{"word":"conserve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɝv/","definition":"to use something carefully so it lasts longer","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد","example":"We should conserve water in the desert.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W04"},{"word":"drought","pos":"noun","ipa":"/draʊt/","definition":"a long time with little or no rain","arabic":"الجفاف","example":"The farmers lost their crops in the drought.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W05"},{"word":"litter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪtɚ/","definition":"rubbish that people drop in public places","arabic":"القمامة الملقاة","example":"Please don't drop litter on the beach.","image_id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"Environment words: environment, pollution, recycle, waste, protect, endangered, species, habitat, climate, renewable, reduce, conserve, drought, litter.\nWord families: -tion / -ion makes nouns (pollute → pollution, protect → protection, conserve → conservation). -al makes adjectives (environment → environmental). -able means \"can be\" (recycle → recyclable, renew → renewable). -ful means \"full of\" (waste → wasteful, harm → harmful). -ly makes adverbs (environmentally).\nThe prefix en- means \"put into\": endanger = put into danger → endangered animals. species is the same in the singular and plural: one species, two species.\nWord families: pollute: pollution (n), polluted (adj) | protect: protection (n), protective (adj) | conserve: conservation (n) | recycle: recycling (n), recyclable (adj), recycled (adj) | environment: environmental (adj), environmentally (adv) | waste: wasteful (adj)\nCollocations/phrases: air / water / plastic pollution • food / plastic waste • climate change | endangered species • natural habitat • renewable energy • solar power | reduce waste • conserve water • protect wildlife • drop litter • recycle bottles","examples":["Air pollution is a problem in big cities.","The river is polluted with chemicals.","Plastic bottles are recyclable.","Leaving the tap running is wasteful.","The Arabian oryx is a protected species.","Environmental groups clean the coral reefs.","Wildlife protection is important in the Red Sea.","An environmentally friendly car uses less fuel."],"common_errors":["✗ The pollute in the city is bad. → ✓ The pollution in the city is bad. (After the → noun.)","✗ This bottle is recycle. → ✓ This bottle is recyclable. (\"can be recycled\" → recyclable.)","✗ The leopard is a danger animal. → ✓ The leopard is an endangered animal. (At risk of disappearing → endangered.)","✗ Some birds are in danger species. → ✓ Some birds are endangered species. (Collocation: endangered species.)"],"arabic":"مفردات البيئة: pollution (التلوث) وhabitat (الموطن) وendangered (مهدد بالانقراض) وrenewable (متجدد) وdrought (الجفاف).\nاللواحق: -tion للاسم (pollution)، و-al للصفة (environmental)، و-able بمعنى «يمكن» (recyclable)، و-ful بمعنى «مليء بـ» (wasteful).\nالبادئة en تعني «يضع في»: endanger = يعرّض للخطر.\nكلمة species مفردها وجمعها بالشكل نفسه."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Pollute, Pollution, Polluted: Environment Word Families”. Let’s learn environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U4-LS3 | Pollute, Pollution, Polluted: Environment Word Families","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. climate: the usual weather in a place over a long time. renewable: coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind. reduce: to make something smaller or less.","on_screen":"climate | renewable | reduce","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Environment words: environment, pollution, recycle, waste, protect, endangered, species, habitat, climate, renewable, reduce, conserve, drought, litter. Word families: -tion / -ion makes nouns (pollute → pollution, protect → protection, conserve → conservation). -al makes adjectives (environment → environmental). -able means \"can be\" (recycle → recyclable, renew → renewable). -ful means \"full of\" (waste → wasteful, harm → harmful). -ly makes adverbs (environmentally).","on_screen":"environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Air pollution is a problem in big cities. The river is polluted with chemicals. Plastic bottles are recyclable.","on_screen":"Air pollution is a problem in big cities. / The river is polluted with chemicals. / Plastic bottles are recyclable.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The pollute in the city is bad.” That’s not right. We say: “The pollution in the city is bad.” After the → noun.","on_screen":"✗ The pollute in the city is bad.   ✓ The pollution in the city is bad.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"recyclable\" means… … Think! … It *can be* recycled. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about environmental problems and solutions.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about environmental problems and solutions.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","مفردات البيئة: pollution (التلوث) وhabitat (الموطن) وendangered (مهدد بالانقراض) وrenewable (متجدد) وdrought (الجفاف).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The pollute in the city is bad. — الصحيح: The pollution in the city is bad.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن مشكلات البيئة وحلولها."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The ___ of the river is killing the fish.","options":["polluting","pollution","pollute","polluted"],"answer":"pollution","explanation":"After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"Glass jars are ___, so don't throw them away.","options":["recycles","recycle","recycling","recyclable"],"answer":"recyclable","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"The sand cat is a protected ___ in Saudi Arabia.","options":["species","specieses","specie","special"],"answer":"species","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"Rangers work hard on the ___ of wildlife.","options":["protection","protective","protect","protected"],"answer":"protection","explanation":"After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"Buying too much food that you throw away is ___.","options":["wasted","waste","wasteful","wastefully"],"answer":"wasteful","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"We must ___ water because our climate is dry.","options":["conservative","conservation","conserve","conserved"],"answer":"conserve","explanation":"After will/can/to → verb.","explanation_ar":"بعد will أو to ← فعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"habitat","options":["coming from a source that doesn't run out","the usual weather in a place over many years","rubbish dropped in public places","the natural home of an animal or plant","at risk of disappearing forever","a long time with very little rain"],"answer":"the natural home of an animal or plant","explanation":"habitat → the natural home of an animal or plant. After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"drought","options":["coming from a source that doesn't run out","the usual weather in a place over many years","rubbish dropped in public places","the natural home of an animal or plant","at risk of disappearing forever","a long time with very little rain"],"answer":"a long time with very little rain","explanation":"drought → a long time with very little rain. After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"renewable","options":["coming from a source that doesn't run out","the usual weather in a place over many years","rubbish dropped in public places","the natural home of an animal or plant","at risk of disappearing forever","a long time with very little rain"],"answer":"coming from a source that doesn't run out","explanation":"renewable → coming from a source that doesn't run out. After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"climate","options":["coming from a source that doesn't run out","the usual weather in a place over many years","rubbish dropped in public places","the natural home of an animal or plant","at risk of disappearing forever","a long time with very little rain"],"answer":"the usual weather in a place over many years","explanation":"climate → the usual weather in a place over many years. After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"litter","options":["coming from a source that doesn't run out","the usual weather in a place over many years","rubbish dropped in public places","the natural home of an animal or plant","at risk of disappearing forever","a long time with very little rain"],"answer":"rubbish dropped in public places","explanation":"litter → rubbish dropped in public places. After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"endangered","options":["coming from a source that doesn't run out","the usual weather in a place over many years","rubbish dropped in public places","the natural home of an animal or plant","at risk of disappearing forever","a long time with very little rain"],"answer":"at risk of disappearing forever","explanation":"endangered → at risk of disappearing forever. After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word families.","items":[{"q":"Write a sentence with \"pollution\".","options":[],"answer":"Plastic pollution is harming sea turtles.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a sentence with \"environmental\".","options":[],"answer":"Our school has an environmental club.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Name something that is recyclable.","options":[],"answer":"Aluminum cans are recyclable.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Name a renewable energy source in Saudi Arabia.","options":[],"answer":"Solar energy is a renewable source in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Describe one wasteful habit you want to stop.","options":[],"answer":"I want to stop the wasteful habit of printing every page.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Problem and solution.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about an environmental problem in your area.","options":[],"answer":"There is a lot of litter in the desert after picnics. Plastic bags are harmful to camels and other animals.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with solutions using conserve, reduce or protect.","options":[],"answer":"We should reduce the use of plastic bags. People should protect the desert by taking their rubbish home.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about an endangered species.","options":[],"answer":"The Arabian leopard is an endangered species, so it needs protection.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"pollution","category":"noun","family":"pollute"},{"word":"polluted","category":"adjective","family":"pollute"},{"word":"protection","category":"noun","family":"protect"},{"word":"protective","category":"adjective","family":"protect"},{"word":"conservation","category":"noun","family":"conserve"},{"word":"recycling","category":"noun","family":"recycle"},{"word":"recyclable","category":"adjective","family":"recycle"},{"word":"recycled","category":"adjective","family":"recycle"},{"word":"environmental","category":"adjective","family":"environment"},{"word":"environmentally","category":"adverb","family":"environment"},{"word":"wasteful","category":"adjective","family":"waste"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The beach was ___ after the holiday; there was rubbish everywhere.","options":["pollutant air","pollution","pollute","polluted"],"answer":"polluted","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"The city started a new ___ program for plastic and paper.","options":["recycling","recyclable","recycle","recycled it"],"answer":"recycling","explanation":"After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"Solar power is an ___ friendly source of energy.","options":["environmentally","environment","environments","environmental"],"answer":"environmentally","explanation":"Before an adjective or describing a verb → adverb (-ly).","explanation_ar":"الظرف."},{"q":"Mangrove forests are an important ___ for birds and fish.","options":["drought","habitat","climate","litter"],"answer":"habitat","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"If we don't protect them, these animals will become ___.","options":["wasteful","recyclable","extinct","renewable"],"answer":"extinct","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"The ___ of water is very important in a desert country.","options":["conservative","conservation","conserved","conserve"],"answer":"conservation","explanation":"After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"Wearing a helmet is a ___ measure.","options":["protect","protection","protectively","protective"],"answer":"protective","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"Please don't drop ___ in the park.","options":["climate","species","habitat","litter"],"answer":"litter","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["Wind and sun are renew sources of energy.","Wind and sun are renewing sources of energy.","Wind and sun are renewable sources of energy.","Wind and sun are renewably sources of energy."],"answer":"Wind and sun are renewable sources of energy.","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"The farmers had no water for their crops during the ___.","options":["habitat","climate","drought","pollution"],"answer":"drought","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A two-sided poster: on the left a polluted beach with litter, smoke and a sad turtle; on the right the same beach clean, with solar panels, recycling bins, a healthy mangrove and a happy turtle. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A two-sided poster: on the left a polluted beach with litter, smoke and a sad turtle; on the right the same beach clean, with solar panels, recycling bins, a healthy mangrove and a happy turtle"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows climate (the usual weather in a place over a long time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing climate: the usual weather in a place over a long time"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows renewable (coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing renewable: coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows reduce (to make something smaller or less); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing reduce: to make something smaller or less"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows conserve (to use something carefully so it lasts longer); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing conserve: to use something carefully so it lasts longer"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows drought (a long time with little or no rain); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing drought: a long time with little or no rain"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows litter (rubbish that people drop in public places); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing litter: rubbish that people drop in public places"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W01","script":"climate. climate. Saudi Arabia has a hot, dry climate.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W02","script":"renewable. renewable. Solar power is a renewable form of energy.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W03","script":"reduce. reduce. Please reduce the amount of plastic you use.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W04","script":"conserve. conserve. We should conserve water in the desert.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W05","script":"drought. drought. The farmers lost their crops in the drought.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-W06","script":"litter. litter. Please don't drop litter on the beach.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Pollute, Pollution, Polluted: Environment Word Families”. Let’s learn environment vocabulary; word families with -tion/-ion, -al, -able, -ful, -ed, -ly; prefix en- (endanger) together. Meet some new words. climate: the usual weather in a place over a long time. renewable: coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind. reduce: to make something smaller or less. Environment words: environment, pollution, recycle, waste, protect, endangered, species, habitat, climate, renewable, reduce, conserve, drought, litter. Word families: -tion / -ion makes nouns (pollute → pollution, protect → protection, conserve → conservation). -al makes adjectives (environment → environmental). -able means \"can be\" (recycle → recyclable, renew → renewable). -ful means \"full of\" (waste → wasteful, harm → harmful). -ly makes adverbs (environmentally). Here are some examples. Air pollution is a problem in big cities. The river is polluted with chemicals. Plastic bottles are recyclable. Be careful! Some learners say: “The pollute in the city is bad.” That’s not right. We say: “The pollution in the city is bad.” After the → noun. Quick check: \"recyclable\" means… … Think! … It *can be* recycled. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about environmental problems and solutions.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4","title":"If It Rains, We'll Stay Inside: Commas in Conditional and Time Sentences","objectives":["Students will be able to use a comma after an if-, unless- or when-clause at the start of a sentence.","Students will be able to leave out the comma when the main clause comes first.","I can write \"If we recycle, we will save trees.\" with a comma.","I can write \"We will save trees if we recycle.\" without a comma."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وضع فاصلة بعد جملة if أو unless أو when في بداية الجملة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من حذف الفاصلة عندما تأتي الجملة الرئيسة أولًا.","أستطيع أن أكتب If we recycle, we will save trees. بفاصلة.","أستطيع أن أكتب We will save trees if we recycle. دون فاصلة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"environment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","definition":"the air, water and land around us where people, animals and plants live","arabic":"البيئة","example":"We must keep our environment clean.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"pollution","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈluʃən/","definition":"dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land","arabic":"التلوّث","example":"Car fumes cause air pollution in big cities.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"recycle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"to treat used things so they can be used again","arabic":"يعيد التدوير","example":"We recycle paper and cans at school.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"waste","pos":"noun","ipa":"/weɪst/","definition":"things we throw away because we don't need them","arabic":"النفايات / الهدر","example":"Restaurants produce a lot of food waste.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"protect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prəˈtɛkt/","definition":"to keep something safe from harm","arabic":"يحمي","example":"Rangers protect the animals in the reserve.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"endangered","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɛnˈdeɪndʒɚd/","definition":"at risk of disappearing forever","arabic":"مهدَّد بالانقراض","example":"The Arabian leopard is an endangered animal.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"When an if-clause or a time clause (when, as soon as, before, after, until, unless) comes first, put a comma after it: If we recycle, we will save trees.\nWhen the main clause comes first, we usually don't use a comma: We will save trees if we recycle.\nRemember the other rules: each sentence starts with a capital letter and ends with a period or a question mark, and an if-clause alone is a fragment: (not: If we recycle.)\nIf/When/Unless + clause, main clause.\nMain clause + if/when/unless + clause (no comma).\nAn if-clause alone is a fragment.\nDon't put the comma right after \"if\" or \"when\".","examples":["If it rains tomorrow, we'll stay inside.","We'll stay inside if it rains tomorrow.","Unless we act now, the coral reefs will die.","The coral reefs will die unless we act now.","As soon as the bell rings, we'll go to the garden.","When the sun sets, the desert gets cold.","Turn off the lights before you leave.","Before you leave, turn off the lights."],"common_errors":["✗ If we plant trees the air will be cleaner. → ✓ If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner. (If-clause first → comma.)","✗ The air will be cleaner, if we plant trees. → ✓ The air will be cleaner if we plant trees. (Main clause first → no comma.)","✗ If, we recycle we will save energy. → ✓ If we recycle, we will save energy. (The comma goes after the whole if-clause.)","✗ Unless we stop wasting water. → ✓ Unless we stop wasting water, we will face a drought. (An unless-clause alone is a fragment.)"],"arabic":"إذا بدأت الجملة بجملة if أو when أو unless نضع فاصلة بعدها: If we recycle, we will save trees.\nإذا جاءت الجملة الرئيسة أولًا لا نضع فاصلة عادة: We will save trees if we recycle.\nالفاصلة تأتي بعد جملة الشرط كاملة، وليس بعد if مباشرة.\nجملة الشرط وحدها جملة ناقصة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If It Rains, We'll Stay Inside: Commas in Conditional and Time Sentences”. Let’s learn commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U4-LS4 | If It Rains, We'll Stay Inside: Commas in Conditional and Time Sentences","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"When an if-clause or a time clause (when, as soon as, before, after, until, unless) comes first, put a comma after it: If we recycle, we will save trees.","on_screen":"commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"When an if-clause or a time clause (when, as soon as, before, after, until, unless) comes first, put a comma after it: If we recycle, we will save trees. When the main clause comes first, we usually don't use a comma: We will save trees if we recycle.","on_screen":"If/When/Unless + clause, main clause. • Main clause + if/when/unless + clause (no comma). • An if-clause alone is a fragment.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. If it rains tomorrow, we'll stay inside. We'll stay inside if it rains tomorrow. Unless we act now, the coral reefs will die.","on_screen":"If it rains tomorrow, we'll stay inside. / We'll stay inside if it rains tomorrow. / Unless we act now, the coral reefs will die.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If we plant trees the air will be cleaner.” That’s not right. We say: “If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner.” If-clause first → comma.","on_screen":"✗ If we plant trees the air will be cleaner.   ✓ If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"If we recycle we will save trees.\" Where does the comma go? … Think! … After *recycle*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"If we recycle, we will save trees.\" with a comma.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"If we recycle, we will save trees.\" with a comma.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","إذا بدأت الجملة بجملة if أو when أو unless نضع فاصلة بعدها: If we recycle, we will save trees.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If we plant trees the air will be cleaner. — الصحيح: If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب If we recycle, we will save trees. بفاصلة."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Green Tips for Our School (editing passage)","body":"If you leave a room turn off the lights. Unless we close the taps we'll waste water. We'll have a cleaner school, if everyone uses the bins. When, the bell rings, collect your bottles. Before you print a page ask yourself if you really need it. Our planet will thank you, if you follow these tips!","word_count":56,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correctly punctuated sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["If we reduce waste the landfill won't grow.","If, we reduce waste the landfill won't grow.","If we reduce waste, the landfill won't grow.","If we reduce, waste the landfill won't grow."],"answer":"If we reduce waste, the landfill won't grow.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The landfill won't grow if we reduce waste.","The landfill won't grow if, we reduce waste.","The landfill won't grow, if we reduce waste.","The landfill, won't grow if we reduce waste."],"answer":"The landfill won't grow if we reduce waste.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["When the rain, stops we'll plant the seeds.","When, the rain stops we'll plant the seeds.","When the rain stops we'll plant the seeds.","When the rain stops, we'll plant the seeds."],"answer":"When the rain stops, we'll plant the seeds.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Unless we protect the reefs the fish will disappear.","Unless we protect the reefs, the fish will disappear.","Unless we protect, the reefs the fish will disappear.","Unless, we protect the reefs the fish will disappear."],"answer":"Unless we protect the reefs, the fish will disappear.","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause, not after \"if\".","explanation_ar":"مكان الفاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Please switch off the fan, before you leave.","Please switch off, the fan before you leave.","Please switch off the fan before, you leave.","Please switch off the fan before you leave."],"answer":"Please switch off the fan before you leave.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"Spot the incomplete sentence.","options":["The fish will return if the factories stop polluting the river.","The factories will stop polluting the river.","If the factories stop polluting the river.","If the factories stop polluting the river, the fish will return."],"answer":"If the factories stop polluting the river.","explanation":"An if/unless/when-clause alone is a fragment.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط وحدها ناقصة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add a comma if needed. Write the sentence.","items":[{"q":"If you see litter pick it up.  (comma)","options":[],"answer":"If you see litter, pick it up.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"The plants will die unless you water them.  (no comma needed)","options":[],"answer":"The plants will die unless you water them.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"As soon as we get the bins we'll start recycling.  (comma)","options":[],"answer":"As soon as we get the bins, we'll start recycling.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Fix the fragment. Add a main clause.","items":[{"q":"If everyone helps.  +  we'll finish quickly","options":[],"answer":"If everyone helps, we'll finish quickly.","explanation":"An if/unless/when-clause alone is a fragment.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"When the volunteers arrive.  +  we'll clean the beach","options":[],"answer":"When the volunteers arrive, we'll clean the beach.","explanation":"An if/unless/when-clause alone is a fragment.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"Unless we save energy.  +  the bills will rise","options":[],"answer":"Unless we save energy, the bills will rise.","explanation":"An if/unless/when-clause alone is a fragment.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط وحدها ناقصة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the Eco Club poster.","items":[{"q":"If you leave a room turn off the lights.","options":[],"answer":"If you leave a room, turn off the lights.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"If you leave a room turn off the lights.","options":[],"answer":"If you leave a room, turn off the lights.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We'll have a cleaner school, if everyone uses the bins. When the bell rings, collect your bottles.","options":[],"answer":"We'll have a cleaner schoolif everyone uses the bins. When the bell rings, collect your bottles.","explanation":", if → if. Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , if → if. جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We'll have a cleaner schoolif everyone uses the bins. When, the bell rings, collect your bottles.","options":[],"answer":"We'll have a cleaner schoolif everyone uses the bins. When the bell rings, collect your bottles.","explanation":"When, the bell → When the bell. Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: When, the bell → When the bell. جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"If you leave a room turn off the lights.","options":[],"answer":"If you leave a room, turn off the lights.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"We'll have a cleaner school, if everyone uses the bins. When the bell rings, collect your bottles.","options":[],"answer":"We'll have a cleaner schoolif everyone uses the bins. When the bell rings, collect your bottles.","explanation":", if → if. Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , if → if. جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your own green tips.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 tips that start with If or When (use a comma).","options":[],"answer":"If you go to the beach, take your rubbish home. When you brush your teeth, turn off the tap.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the same 2 tips with the main clause first (no comma).","options":[],"answer":"Take your rubbish home if you go to the beach. Turn off the tap when you brush your teeth.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one warning that starts with Unless.","options":[],"answer":"Unless we plant more trees, our cities will get hotter.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"environment","clue":"the air, water and land around us where people, animals and plants live"},{"word":"pollution","clue":"dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land"},{"word":"species","clue":"a group of animals or plants of the same kind"},{"word":"renewable","clue":"coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind"},{"word":"conserve","clue":"to use something carefully so it lasts longer"},{"word":"drought","clue":"a long time with little or no rain"},{"word":"recycle","clue":"to treat used things so they can be used again"},{"word":"waste","clue":"things we throw away because we don't need them"},{"word":"protect","clue":"to keep something safe from harm"},{"word":"endangered","clue":"at risk of disappearing forever"},{"word":"habitat","clue":"the natural home of an animal or plant"},{"word":"climate","clue":"the usual weather in a place over a long time"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["If the school buys solar panels it will save money.","If the school buys solar panels, it will save money.","If the school buys, solar panels it will save money.","If, the school buys solar panels it will save money."],"answer":"If the school buys solar panels, it will save money.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We'll go to the reserve if, the weather is good.","We'll go to the reserve, if the weather is good.","We'll go to the reserve if the weather is good.","We'll go, to the reserve if the weather is good."],"answer":"We'll go to the reserve if the weather is good.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"As soon as the sun rises the panels will start working.\"","options":["after sun","after panels","after rises","after soon"],"answer":"after rises","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause, not after \"if\".","explanation_ar":"مكان الفاصلة."},{"q":"Does this sentence need a comma? \"The lake will dry up unless it rains.\"","options":["Yes, after unless.","Yes, after up.","Yes, after lake.","No, the main clause comes first."],"answer":"No, the main clause comes first.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Before you go, camping check the weather forecast.","Before, you go camping check the weather forecast.","Before you go camping check the weather forecast.","Before you go camping, check the weather forecast."],"answer":"Before you go camping, check the weather forecast.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"What is wrong with \"When we finish the cleanup.\"?","options":["It's a fragment.","Nothing is wrong.","It has too many commas.","It needs a question mark."],"answer":"It's a fragment.","explanation":"An if/unless/when-clause alone is a fragment.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"","options":["Unless people stop hunting, the gazelles will disappear.","Unless people stop hunting the gazelles will disappear.","Unless people stop, hunting the gazelles will disappear.","Unless, people stop hunting the gazelles will disappear."],"answer":"Unless people stop hunting, the gazelles will disappear.","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause, not after \"if\".","explanation_ar":"مكان الفاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The air will be cleaner, if more people ride buses.","The air will be cleaner if more people ride buses.","The air, will be cleaner if more people ride buses.","The air will be cleaner if more people, ride buses."],"answer":"The air will be cleaner if more people ride buses.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"How many commas does this sentence need? \"If we plant trees they will give us shade.\"","options":["two","three","none","one"],"answer":"one","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["When the dust storm ends, we'll open the windows.","When the dust storm, ends we'll open the windows.","When the dust storm ends we'll open the windows.","When, the dust storm ends we'll open the windows."],"answer":"When the dust storm ends, we'll open the windows.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Our Planet” that shows commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Our Planet” that shows commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first in action"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “If It Rains, We'll Stay Inside: Commas in Conditional and Time Sentences”. Let’s learn commas after an introductory if-, unless- or time clause; no comma when the main clause comes first together. When an if-clause or a time clause (when, as soon as, before, after, until, unless) comes first, put a comma after it: If we recycle, we will save trees. When an if-clause or a time clause (when, as soon as, before, after, until, unless) comes first, put a comma after it: If we recycle, we will save trees. When the main clause comes first, we usually don't use a comma: We will save trees if we recycle. Here are some examples. If it rains tomorrow, we'll stay inside. We'll stay inside if it rains tomorrow. Unless we act now, the coral reefs will die. Be careful! Some learners say: “If we plant trees the air will be cleaner.” That’s not right. We say: “If we plant trees, the air will be cleaner.” If-clause first → comma. Quick check: \"If we recycle we will save trees.\" Where does the comma go? … Think! … After *recycle*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"If we recycle, we will save trees.\" with a comma.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5","title":"Our Eco Pledge: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to discuss environmental problems and propose solutions with conditionals and time clauses.","Students will be able to write a persuasive eco letter with correct punctuation.","I can make an eco pledge with my class.","I can write a letter to my principal about a green project."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مناقشة مشكلات البيئة واقتراح الحلول بالجمل الشرطية وجمل الزمن.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة رسالة بيئية إقناعية بترقيم صحيح.","أستطيع أن أكتب تعهدًا بيئيًا مع صفي.","أستطيع أن أكتب رسالة إلى مدير مدرستي عن مشروع أخضر."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"environment","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","definition":"the air, water and land around us where people, animals and plants live","arabic":"البيئة","example":"We must keep our environment clean.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"pollution","pos":"noun","ipa":"/pəˈluʃən/","definition":"dirty or harmful things in the air, water or land","arabic":"التلوّث","example":"Car fumes cause air pollution in big cities.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"recycle","pos":"verb","ipa":"/riˈsaɪkəl/","definition":"to treat used things so they can be used again","arabic":"يعيد التدوير","example":"We recycle paper and cans at school.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"waste","pos":"noun","ipa":"/weɪst/","definition":"things we throw away because we don't need them","arabic":"النفايات / الهدر","example":"Restaurants produce a lot of food waste.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"protect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/prəˈtɛkt/","definition":"to keep something safe from harm","arabic":"يحمي","example":"Rangers protect the animals in the reserve.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"endangered","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɛnˈdeɪndʒɚd/","definition":"at risk of disappearing forever","arabic":"مهدَّد بالانقراض","example":"The Arabian leopard is an endangered animal.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"species","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈspiʃiz/","definition":"a group of animals or plants of the same kind","arabic":"نوع / فصيلة","example":"Scientists found a new species of lizard.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"habitat","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhæbəˌtæt/","definition":"the natural home of an animal or plant","arabic":"موطن طبيعي","example":"The desert is the habitat of the Arabian oryx.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"climate","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈklaɪmət/","definition":"the usual weather in a place over a long time","arabic":"المناخ","example":"Saudi Arabia has a hot, dry climate.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"renewable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/riˈnuəbəl/","definition":"coming from a source that doesn't run out, like the sun or wind","arabic":"متجدّد","example":"Solar power is a renewable form of energy.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"reduce","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rəˈdus/","definition":"to make something smaller or less","arabic":"يقلّل","example":"Please reduce the amount of plastic you use.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"conserve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/kənˈsɝv/","definition":"to use something carefully so it lasts longer","arabic":"يحافظ على / يرشّد","example":"We should conserve water in the desert.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"drought","pos":"noun","ipa":"/draʊt/","definition":"a long time with little or no rain","arabic":"الجفاف","example":"The farmers lost their crops in the drought.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"litter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈlɪtɚ/","definition":"rubbish that people drop in public places","arabic":"القمامة الملقاة","example":"Please don't drop litter on the beach.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families and commas in conditional sentences.\nA persuasive letter states the problem, gives the results (if…, …will), adds a warning (unless…) and a plan (as soon as…, when…).\n✔ If + present simple, will + base verb\n✔ unless = if not • when (sure) vs if (possible)\n✔ when / as soon as / before / until + present simple\n✔ comma after an introductory if / when / unless clause","examples":["If we put bins in every class, students will recycle more.","Unless we act quickly, the yard will stay dirty.","When the new term starts, we'll launch the project.","As soon as we collect 500 bottles, we'll take them to the recycling center.","Plastic pollution is harmful to sea animals.","The project is environmentally friendly.","We'll keep working until every class joins us.","Water conservation is important in a dry climate."],"common_errors":["✗ If we will recycle, we will help the planet. → ✓ If we recycle, we will help the planet. (No will after if.)","✗ As soon as the panels will arrive we will start. → ✓ As soon as the panels arrive, we will start. (Present simple + comma.)","✗ This is very pollution. → ✓ This causes a lot of pollution. / The air is very polluted. (Noun vs adjective.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الجملة الشرطية الأولى وunless وwhen وif وجمل الزمن ومفردات البيئة والفاصلة في الجمل الشرطية.\nالرسالة الإقناعية تذكر المشكلة، ثم النتائج (If…, …will)، ثم التحذير (Unless…)، ثم الخطة (As soon as…).\nتذكّر: لا will بعد if أو when، وفاصلة بعد جملة الشرط في البداية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Eco Pledge: Language in Use”. Let’s learn first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U4-LS5 | Our Eco Pledge: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Eco council debate: in groups, choose one problem (water waste, plastic, energy, litter). Present 3 first-conditional results, one unless-warning and one plan with as soon as / when. The class votes for the best project.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 4: the first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families and commas in conditional sentences. A persuasive letter states the problem, gives the results (if…, …will), adds a warning (unless…) and a plan (as soon as…, when…).","on_screen":"✔ If + present simple, will + base verb • ✔ unless = if not • when (sure) vs if (possible) • ✔ when / as soon as / before / until + present simple","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. If we put bins in every class, students will recycle more. Unless we act quickly, the yard will stay dirty. When the new term starts, we'll launch the project.","on_screen":"If we put bins in every class, students will recycle more. / Unless we act quickly, the yard will stay dirty. / When the new term starts, we'll launch the project.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “If we will recycle, we will help the planet.” That’s not right. We say: “If we recycle, we will help the planet.” No will after if.","on_screen":"✗ If we will recycle, we will help the planet.   ✓ If we recycle, we will help the planet.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “As soon as the panels will arrive we will start.”? … Think! … It should be “As soon as the panels arrive, we will start.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can make an eco pledge with my class.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can make an eco pledge with my class.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الجملة الشرطية الأولى وunless وwhen وif وجمل الزمن ومفردات البيئة والفاصلة في الجمل الشرطية.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: If we will recycle, we will help the planet. — الصحيح: If we recycle, we will help the planet.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب تعهدًا بيئيًا مع صفي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class","body":"Dear Mr. Khalid,\nWe are writing to ask for solar panels on our school roof.\nOur school uses a lot of electricity for air conditioning, and this is wasteful.\nIf we install solar panels, the school will save money and reduce pollution.\nSolar energy is renewable, so it won't run out.\nUnless we change our energy habits, our bills will keep rising.\nAs soon as the panels arrive, our Eco Club will make posters to explain the project.\nIf you agree, we will be very proud of our environmentally friendly school.\nYours sincerely, Lina's Class","word_count":95,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the letter. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The class wants solar panels on the school roof.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The school doesn't use much electricity.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Solar panels will help the school save money.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Solar energy will run out one day.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The Eco Club will make posters when the panels arrive.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The letter is addressed to Mr. Khalid.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “A Letter to Our Principal – Lina's Class”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"If we install solar panels, the school ___ money.","options":["will save","saves","saved","saving"],"answer":"will save","explanation":"First conditional (If + present, will + base).","explanation_ar":"الشرطية الأولى."},{"q":"___ we change our habits, our bills will keep rising.","options":["When","If","Unless","As soon as"],"answer":"Unless","explanation":"unless = if not.","explanation_ar":"unless."},{"q":"As soon as the panels ___, the Eco Club will make posters.","options":["arrived","arrive","will arrive","arriving"],"answer":"arrive","explanation":"when/as soon as/before/until + present simple.","explanation_ar":"جمل الزمن."},{"q":"Solar energy is ___, so it won't run out.","options":["renewable","renewal","renew","renewably"],"answer":"renewable","explanation":"Environment word or word-family form.","explanation_ar":"كلمة البيئة."},{"q":"Using too much electricity is ___.","options":["wastefully","wasted","wasteful","waste"],"answer":"wasteful","explanation":"Environment word or word-family form.","explanation_ar":"كلمة البيئة."},{"q":"","options":["If, you agree we will be very proud.","If you agree we will be very proud.","If you agree we, will be very proud.","If you agree, we will be very proud."],"answer":"If you agree, we will be very proud.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory clause.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Prepare your eco council presentation.","items":[{"q":"Our problem: ___","options":[],"answer":"Our problem is food waste in the school cafeteria.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Result 1 (If…): ___","options":[],"answer":"If students take only what they need, we will reduce food waste.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Result 2 (If…): ___","options":[],"answer":"If we give the extra food to a charity, families in need will get it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Warning (Unless…): ___","options":[],"answer":"Unless we act, tons of food will go into the garbage.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Plan (As soon as / When…): ___","options":[],"answer":"As soon as the principal agrees, we'll put up signs in the cafeteria.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your letter to the principal.","items":[{"q":"Plan: problem, 2 if-results, unless-warning, time-clause plan, polite ending.","options":[],"answer":"problem: plastic bottles; if-results: buy water fountains – less plastic; reusable bottles – save money; unless: the bins will overflow; plan: as soon as the fountains arrive, we'll give every student a bottle","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your letter in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Dear Mr. Khalid, We are writing about plastic bottles in our school. Every day, students throw away hundreds of bottles. If the school buys water fountains, we will use less plastic. If every student has a reusable bottle, families will save money. Unless we act now, our bins will overflow. As soon as the fountains arrive, we'll give every student a bottle. Thank you for reading our letter. Yours sincerely, Grade 7B","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: no will after if/when? commas? word forms? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"When the fountains will arrive we'll start\" to \"When the fountains arrive, we'll start\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"environment","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"pollution","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"recycle","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"waste","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"protect","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"endangered","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"species","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"habitat","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"climate","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"renewable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"reduce","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"conserve","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"drought","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"litter","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"If people ___ the desert clean, the animals will be safe.","options":["keep","will keep","kept","keeping"],"answer":"keep","explanation":"First conditional (If + present, will + base).","explanation_ar":"الشرطية الأولى."},{"q":"","options":["Unless we will save energy, the planet will get warmer.","Unless we save energy, the planet will get warmer.","Unless we don't save energy, the planet will get warmer.","Unless we saved energy, the planet will get warmer."],"answer":"Unless we save energy, the planet will get warmer.","explanation":"unless = if not.","explanation_ar":"unless."},{"q":"___ the new term starts, we'll start the recycling project.","options":["If","Until","When","Unless"],"answer":"When","explanation":"when/as soon as/before/until + present simple.","explanation_ar":"جمل الزمن."},{"q":"We'll keep cleaning ___ the beach is spotless.","options":["until","if not","unless","as soon"],"answer":"until","explanation":"when/as soon as/before/until + present simple.","explanation_ar":"جمل الزمن."},{"q":"The ___ of energy saves money and helps the planet.","options":["conserved","conservative","conserve","conservation"],"answer":"conservation","explanation":"Environment word or word-family form.","explanation_ar":"كلمة البيئة."},{"q":"Plastic bags are ___ to sea turtles.","options":["harmfully","harmed","harm","harmful"],"answer":"harmful","explanation":"Environment word or word-family form.","explanation_ar":"كلمة البيئة."},{"q":"","options":["When the volunteers arrive, we'll start planting.","When, the volunteers arrive we'll start planting.","When the volunteers, arrive we'll start planting.","When the volunteers arrive we'll start planting."],"answer":"When the volunteers arrive, we'll start planting.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory clause.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The coral reef recovers tomorrow if we stop polluting the sea.","The coral reef will recover, if we stop polluting the sea.","The coral reef will recover if we stop polluting the sea.","The coral reef will recover if we will stop polluting the sea."],"answer":"The coral reef will recover if we stop polluting the sea.","explanation":"Comma after an introductory clause.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة."},{"q":"If the rains don't come this year, there ___ a drought.","options":["be","will be","is","was"],"answer":"will be","explanation":"First conditional (If + present, will + base).","explanation_ar":"الشرطية الأولى."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an eco letter:","options":["If the school plants twenty trees the playground is cooler tomorrow.","If the school will plant twenty trees, the playground will be cooler and greener.","If the school plants twenty trees, the playground will be more cool and green.","If the school plants twenty trees, the playground will be cooler and greener."],"answer":"If the school plants twenty trees, the playground will be cooler and greener.","explanation":"First conditional (If + present, will + base).","explanation_ar":"الشرطية الأولى."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A class eco-pledge banner with students' handprints in green paint, a letter to the principal on a desk, and a model of a school roof with solar panels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A class eco-pledge banner with students' handprints in green paint, a letter to the principal on a desk, and a model of a school roof with solar panels"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Our Planet”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Our Planet”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L05-U4-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS5-T1","script":"Dear Mr. Khalid, We are writing to ask for solar panels on our school roof. Our school uses a lot of electricity for air conditioning, and this is wasteful. If we install solar panels, the school will save money and reduce pollution. Solar energy is renewable, so it won't run out. Unless we change our energy habits, our bills will keep rising. As soon as the panels arrive, our Eco Club will make posters to explain the project. If you agree, we will be very proud of our environmentally friendly school. Yours sincerely, Lina's Class","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U4-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Eco Pledge: Language in Use”. Let’s learn first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families, commas in conditionals (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Eco council debate: in groups, choose one problem (water waste, plastic, energy, litter). Present 3 first-conditional results, one unless-warning and one plan with as soon as / when. The class votes for the best project. Today you use all of Unit 4: the first conditional, unless, when vs if, future time clauses, environment word families and commas in conditional sentences. A persuasive letter states the problem, gives the results (if…, …will), adds a warning (unless…) and a plan (as soon as…, when…). Here are some examples. If we put bins in every class, students will recycle more. Unless we act quickly, the yard will stay dirty. When the new term starts, we'll launch the project. Be careful! Some learners say: “If we will recycle, we will help the planet.” That’s not right. We say: “If we recycle, we will help the planet.” No will after if. Quick check: what is wrong with “As soon as the panels will arrive we will start.”? … Think! … It should be “As soon as the panels arrive, we will start.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can make an eco pledge with my class.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"If we ___ the lights off, we'll save energy.","options":["will turn","turn","turned","turning"],"answer":"turn","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"The sea turtles will die if people ___ plastic into the sea.","options":["will throw","throwing","throw","threw"],"answer":"throw","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"If the river gets polluted, the fish ___.","options":["die tomorrow","will die","died","dying"],"answer":"will die","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."},{"q":"___ we protect the reefs, we'll lose them forever.","options":["If","Unless","As soon as","When"],"answer":"Unless","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"","options":["Unless it doesn't rain soon, the crops will fail.","Unless it rained soon, the crops will fail.","Unless it rains soon, the crops will fail.","Unless it will rain soon, the crops will fail."],"answer":"Unless it rains soon, the crops will fail.","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"What will happen if all the ice ___?","options":["melts","melted","will melt","melting"],"answer":"melts","explanation":"Questions: What will happen if…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال."},{"q":"___ I finish school, I'll study environmental science.","options":["If","Unless","Until","When"],"answer":"When","explanation":"Sure to happen → when.","explanation_ar":"المؤكد ← when."},{"q":"___ the weather is nice tomorrow, we'll go to the reserve. (Maybe it will be.)","options":["Until","When","Before","If"],"answer":"If","explanation":"Might happen → if.","explanation_ar":"المحتمل ← if."},{"q":"We'll wait inside ___ the sandstorm passes.","options":["as soon","if","until","unless"],"answer":"until","explanation":"until = up to the time when.","explanation_ar":"until حتى."},{"q":"","options":["As soon as I get home, I sort the recycling yesterday.","As soon as I will get home, I'll sort the recycling.","As soon as I got home, I'll sort the recycling.","As soon as I get home, I'll sort the recycling."],"answer":"As soon as I get home, I'll sort the recycling.","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Before you ___ the tent, check for scorpions.","options":["opened","will open","opening","open"],"answer":"open","explanation":"After when/as soon as/before/after/until → present simple.","explanation_ar":"بعد كلمات الزمن ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Air ___ is a big problem in many large cities.","options":["pollution","pollute","polluted","polluting"],"answer":"pollution","explanation":"After the/a/an or as a subject → noun.","explanation_ar":"بعد أداة التعريف ← اسم."},{"q":"This plastic box is ___, so put it in the blue bin.","options":["recycling","recycles","recyclable","recycle"],"answer":"recyclable","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"Our school has started an ___ club.","options":["environmentally","environmental","environment","environments"],"answer":"environmental","explanation":"Before a noun or after be → adjective.","explanation_ar":"قبل الاسم ← صفة."},{"q":"The Arabian oryx is a ___ that almost disappeared.","options":["climate","species","habitat","drought"],"answer":"species","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"A long period without rain is called a ___.","options":["drought","litter","species","habitat"],"answer":"drought","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"Wind power is a ___ source of energy.","options":["wasteful","polluted","endangered","renewable"],"answer":"renewable","explanation":"Choose the environment word with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"المعنى الصحيح."},{"q":"","options":["If we recycle more paper we'll, cut down fewer trees.","If, we recycle more paper we'll cut down fewer trees.","If we recycle more paper, we'll cut down fewer trees.","If we recycle more paper we'll cut down fewer trees."],"answer":"If we recycle more paper, we'll cut down fewer trees.","explanation":"Clause with if/when/unless first → comma after it.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط أولًا ← فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["We'll cut down fewer trees if, we recycle more paper.","We'll cut down fewer trees, if we recycle more paper.","We'll cut down, fewer trees if we recycle more paper.","We'll cut down fewer trees if we recycle more paper."],"answer":"We'll cut down fewer trees if we recycle more paper.","explanation":"Main clause first → no comma.","explanation_ar":"الجملة الرئيسة أولًا ← لا فاصلة."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"Unless we act now the leopard will disappear.\"","options":["after leopard","after now","after act","after Unless"],"answer":"after now","explanation":"The comma goes after the whole clause, not after \"if\".","explanation_ar":"مكان الفاصلة."},{"q":"What is wrong with \"If everyone helps clean the park.\"?","options":["It's a fragment.","It needs a question mark.","It has too many commas.","Nothing is wrong."],"answer":"It's a fragment.","explanation":"An if/unless/when-clause alone is a fragment.","explanation_ar":"جملة الشرط وحدها ناقصة."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a persuasive eco letter.","options":["Unless we reduce plastic, our beaches will be covered in litter, so please support our project.","Unless we reduce plastic, our beaches covered in litter, so please support our project.","Unless we don't reduce plastic our beaches will be covered in litter so please support our project.","If we will reduce plastic, our beaches are clean, so please support our project."],"answer":"Unless we reduce plastic, our beaches will be covered in litter, so please support our project.","explanation":"unless = if not (positive verb after it).","explanation_ar":"unless = إذا لم."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"if it will be sunny we will clean the beach.\"","options":["If it is sunny we will clean the beach.","If it will be sunny, we will clean the beach.","If it is sunny, we will clean the beach.","if it is sunny, we will clean the beach."],"answer":"If it is sunny, we will clean the beach.","explanation":"If-clause → present simple (no will).","explanation_ar":"بعد if ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"What will you do if you see someone wasting water? – ___","options":["I'll politely ask him to turn off the tap.","I'll politely asking him to turn off the tap.","I will to ask him politely to turn off the tap.","I politely ask him yesterday to turn off the tap."],"answer":"I'll politely ask him to turn off the tap.","explanation":"Result clause → will / won't + base verb.","explanation_ar":"جملة النتيجة ← will."}],"theme_ar":"كوكبنا","essential_question_ar":"ماذا سيحدث لكوكبنا إذا لم نغيّر عاداتنا؟","can_do":"I can talk about real future possibilities and their results with the first conditional, unless, when and time clauses, use environment word families, and punctuate conditional sentences correctly.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الاحتمالات المستقبلية الحقيقية ونتائجها بالجملة الشرطية الأولى وunless وwhen وجمل الزمن، وأستخدم عائلات كلمات البيئة، وأضع الفاصلة في الجمل الشرطية بشكل صحيح."});
